---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FAQBlock from '../components/FAQBlock.astro';
import RelatedArticles from '../components/RelatedArticles.astro';
import CourseCTA from '../components/CourseCTA.astro';

export const title = "Camera Sensor Cleaning and Maintenance Guide (2026)";
export const category = "camera";
export const description = "Camera sensor cleaning aur maintenance ka complete guide — dust spots kaise identify karein, safe cleaning methods, aur kab professional service leni chahiye.";
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>

<header>
  <h1>Camera Sensor Cleaning and Maintenance Guide</h1>
  <p class="hero-subtitle">Sensor pe dust spots footage mein visible artifacts create kar sakte hain, especially narrow apertures pe. Yeh guide batata hai dust kaise identify karein, kaunse safe cleaning methods hain, aur kab DIY cleaning avoid karke professional service lena better hai.</p>
</header>

<article class="wrap">

  <div class="callout"><b>Quick take:</b> Interchangeable lens cameras mein sensor pe dust jama hona normal hai. Built-in sensor cleaning feature regularly use karo, aur agar dust persist kare, careful blower/swab cleaning karo — ya risk avoid karne ke liye professional service lo.</div>

  <h2>Sensor Pe Dust Kaise Aata Hai</h2>
  <p>Har baar jab aap lens change karte ho, camera body ke andar thodi der ke liye sensor exposed hota hai environment ke liye. Dust particles, especially outdoor ya dusty locations mein, is exposure ke dauran sensor pe settle ho sakte hain. Yeh interchangeable lens cameras (DSLR, mirrorless) ka natural trade-off hai — fixed-lens cameras is issue se largely immune hoti hain.</p>

  <h2>Dust Spots Ko Kaise Identify Karein</h2>
  <p>Sabse reliable test hai: apni camera ko narrow aperture (f/16 ya f/22) pe set karo, ek plain, evenly-lit background (jaise clear sky ya plain white wall) shoot karo, aur image ko zoom karke inspect karo. Dust spots consistent, same-position dark/blurry dots ke roop mein dikhenge — agar aap lens change karke bhi same position pe spots dekhte ho, yeh confirm karta hai ki dust sensor pe hai, lens pe nahi.</p>

  <h2>Level 1: Built-in Sensor Cleaning Feature</h2>
  <p>Zyaadatar modern mirrorless cameras mein ek built-in sensor-shake/vibration cleaning feature hota hai jo power-on/off ke waqt automatically activate hota hai, ya menu se manually trigger kiya ja sakta hai. Yeh first line of defense hai — regularly use karo, especially dusty environment mein shoot karne ke baad.</p>

  <h2>Level 2: Air Blower (Safest DIY Method)</h2>
  <p>Agar built-in cleaning kaafi nahi hai, ek dedicated camera air blower (rubber bulb blower, canned air NAHI) use karo:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Camera ko sensor-cleaning mode mein set karo (mirror/shutter lock ho jaayega open position mein)</li>
    <li>Camera ko slightly downward-facing angle pe hold karo taaki loosened dust bahar gir sake, sensor mein aur na jaaye</li>
    <li>Blower se gentle puffs of air do sensor ke seedha upar se, bina nozzle ko sensor ko touch kiye</li>
    <li>Kabhi bhi canned/compressed air use na karo — pressure bahut zyada hota hai jo sensor ko damage kar sakta hai, aur propellant residue bhi chhod sakta hai</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Level 3: Sensor Swab Cleaning (Advanced, Risky)</h2>
  <p>Agar blower se dust remove nahi hota (aksar yeh oily smudges ya stuck particles hote hain, sirf loose dust nahi), sensor swab aur cleaning solution use kiya ja sakta hai — lekin yeh method sabse zyada risk carry karta hai agar galat tarike se kiya jaaye.</p>
  <div class="callout"><b>Warning:</b> Sensor swab cleaning mein sensor ko physically touch karna involve hota hai. Agar aap confident nahi ho is process mein, professional cleaning service lena zyada safe hai — ek scratched sensor repair se kaafi zyada costly hota hai ek professional cleaning se.</div>

  <h2>Kab Professional Service Lena Chahiye</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Agar dust spots persist karte hain blower cleaning ke baad bhi</li>
    <li>Agar aapko oily smudges ya stubborn marks dikhte hain (yeh aksar lens/body internal lubricant se aate hain)</li>
    <li>Agar aap DIY swab cleaning mein confident nahi ho</li>
    <li>High-value professional bodies ke liye — risk-reward professional service ke favor mein hota hai</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Sensor Dust Se Bachne Ke Preventive Tips</h2>
  <h3>1. Lens Change Karte Waqt Camera Ko Downward Point Karo</h3>
  <p>Gravity ki wajah se dust particles sensor mein settle hone ke bajaye neeche gir jaate hain.</p>
  <h3>2. Body Cap Aur Rear Lens Cap Hamesha Lagao</h3>
  <p>Jab lens ya body use mein nahi hai, caps lagana dust exposure minimize karta hai.</p>
  <h3>3. Dusty/Windy Environments Mein Lens Change Avoid Karo</h3>
  <p>Agar possible ho, indoor ya sheltered location mein lens swap karo outdoor dusty conditions ke bajaye.</p>
  <h3>4. Regular Built-in Cleaning Cycle Chalao</h3>
  <p>Zyaadatar cameras mein yeh automatically har power-on/off pe hota hai — is feature ko disable mat karo.</p>

  <h2>Overall Camera Maintenance Checklist</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sensor: Regular built-in cleaning + periodic manual check</li>
    <li>Lens elements: Microfiber cloth + lens cleaning solution, never rough fabric</li>
    <li>Body exterior: Soft brush ya slightly damp cloth for dust/grime</li>
    <li>Battery contacts: Dry cloth se occasionally wipe karo corrosion avoid karne ke liye</li>
    <li>Storage: Silica gel packets ke saath dry bag mein store karo, especially humid climates mein</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQBlock items={[
    {q: "Sensor pe dust normal hai kya?", a: "Haan, interchangeable lens cameras mein yeh common hai, especially lens changes ke baad. Regular cleaning se manage kiya ja sakta hai."},
    {q: "Kya main khud sensor clean kar sakta hoon?", a: "Blower se basic cleaning safely ki ja sakti hai. Swab cleaning risky hai agar experience nahi hai — professional service consider karo."},
    {q: "Sensor dust footage mein kaise dikhta hai?", a: "Narrow apertures (f/16+) pe consistent dark spots ke roop mein, especially plain backgrounds jaise sky ya wall shots mein noticeable."},
    {q: "Kitni baar sensor clean karna chahiye?", a: "No fixed schedule hai — jab bhi dust spots noticeable ho jaayein footage mein, ya har environment change ke baad periodically check karo."}
  ]} />

